The '''MC80A ''Home One'' Type Heavy Star Cruiser''',<ref name="Starships and Speeders" /> also known as the '''MC80A star cruiser''',<ref name="AB Update">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref><ref name="Starfighters" /> or '''MC80a cruiser''',<ref name="S&V6">{{ShipsandVehiclesCite|6|Pilots and Crew Members}}</ref> was a variant of [[MC80 Star Cruiser]] used by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] and [[New Republic]]. During the [[Galactic Civil War]], several of these ships participated in battles such as [[Battle of Endor|Endor]]<ref name="Episode VI" /> and [[Battle of Jakku|Jakku]].<ref name="Battlefront">''[[Star Wars Battlefront]]''</ref> Around 30 [[Standard year|years]] after the Battle of Endor, the MC80A Star Cruiser was still used by the [[Resistance]].<ref name="BTA" />

One famous example was the ship ''[[Home One]]'', which was a modified version of the MC80A Star Cruiser, and the most advanced vessel in the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]].<ref name="AB Update" />

==History==
===Meeting over Dantooine===
After [[Operation Handoff]], [[Mon Mothma]] abandoned the [[Imperial Senate]] following the [[Ghorman Massacre]], and called on all rebel cells to come together and form the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. Several ships, including ''[[Home One]]'', responded to the call and came to [[Dantooine]].<ref name="Secret Cargo">{{Rebels|Secret Cargo}}</ref>

Shortly thereafter, the [[Telaris rebel stardocks]] began converting and retrofitting ''Home One'' and ''Nautilian'' MC80A star cruisers, along with the [[MC75 Star Cruiser]] the ''[[Profundity]]''. [[Colonel]] [[Anj Zavor]] of [[Rebel Fleet Command]] sent a report to [[Commander-in-Chief]] Mon Mothma, updating her on operations.<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref> By [[1 BBY]],<ref name="RO Date">{{FilmDate|RO}}</ref> the ships had been made battle-ready but were held back until they were ready for war. After the [[battle of Scarif]], which resulted in the death of admiral [[Raddus]] and the loss of most of the rebel fleet, including the ''Profundity'', but also the acquisition of the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[Death Star plans|plans]], Gial Ackbar was appointed the new leader of the Alliance Fleet and made ''Home One'' the new flagship of the fleet.<ref name="Rebel Files" />

===Mutiny on Mon Cala===
Several MC80A cruisers were in service of the [[Mon Cala Mercantile Fleet]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]], which was affiliated with the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Star Wars 44" /> When King [[Lee-Char]] was killed by [[stormtrooper]]s, the fleet and its crew rose against the Imperials onboard their ships.<ref name="SW 48">[[Star Wars (2015) 48|''Star Wars'' (2015) 48]]</ref> As the fleet attempted to escape, the Imperial blockade of six [[Imperial II-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial II''-class Star Destroyers]] prevented them from escaping. [[Luke Skywalker]], [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], [[Chewbacca]], and [[Han Solo]] joined the fleet to help out, as did Gial Ackbar with several squadrons of [[T-65B X-wing starfighter]]s and [[BTL-A4 Y-wing assault starfighter/bomber|BTL-A4 Y-wing assault starfighters]]. The MC80A cruiser ''[[Aurora Flare]]'' rammed into Admiral [[Tyrus Meori]]'s Star Destroyer, creating a pathway and allowing the ships to flee the system to join the Alliance.<ref name="SW 49">[[Star Wars (2015) 49|''Star Wars'' (2015) 49]]</ref>

===Assault on the Mako-Ta Space Docks===
Despite acquiring countless new starships for the Alliance Fleet, the Mon Calamari vessels had yet to become combat-ready warships and still required extensive modifications, such as proper armament, shielding, and hyperdrives. Queen [[Trios]] offered the [[Mako-Ta Space Docks]] and several Shu-Torun engineers to assist the new fleet in retrofitting the ships.<ref name="Star Wars 50">[[Star Wars (2015) 50|''Star Wars'' (2015) 50]]</ref> This turned out to be a trap, as [[Death Squadron]], led by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], entered the system. The cruisers' hyperdrives weren't functioning, and the starfighter bay doors were locked, betrayed by Trios.<ref name="Star Wars 51">[[Star Wars (2015) 51|''Star Wars'' (2015) 51]]</ref> The Alliance scrambled but managed to break free of the malfunctions. While the rest of the fleet escaped, including ''Home One'', [[Jan Dodonna]]'s MC80A cruiser, the [[Republic (MC80A Home One Type Heavy Star Cruiser)|''Republic'']], was destroyed.<ref name="SW 55">[[Star Wars (2015) 55|''Star Wars'' (2015) 55]]</ref>

===Battle of Endor===
After the Empire discovered and destroyed the main Alliance headquarters on [[Hoth]], ''Home One'' served as a mobile command center. The cruiser hosted much of the Alliance's leaders, including Mon Mothma and [[Crix Madine]]. The planning of the battle of [[Endor]] took place here. Utilizing the secret hyperspace route known as the [[Sanctuary Pipeline]],<ref name="Moving Target">''[[Moving Target: A Princess Leia Adventure]]''</ref> ''Home One'' led the Rebel fleet, consisting of at least eight MC80A cruisers, including the ''[[Nautilian]]''<ref name="Life Debt">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref> and ''[[Independence]]'',<ref name="Starfighters">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles]]''</ref> into the system. The fleet battled the largest known Imperial fleet. Despite being heavily outnumbered, the Alliance fleet destroyed the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|second Death Star]], along with a large part of the Imperial fleet. However, they lost several ships, including the ''Nautilian''.

===New Republic service===
After the Battle of Endor, the Alliance to Restore the Republic had reformed into the [[New Republic]], and the MC80A star cruisers continued being used within the [[New Republic Defense Fleet]]. The MC80A was used in battles such as [[Defense of Kuat|Kuat]]<ref name="Blade Squadron: Kuat">{{InsiderCite|168|Blade Squadron: Kuat}}</ref> and [[Liberation of Kashyyyk|Kashyyyk]].<ref name="Life Debt" /> The final battle of the Galactic Civil War was the [[Battle of Jakku]], where at least one ship, ''Home One'', participated. Admiral Ackbar coordinated the battle with other New Republic commanders including Commodore Kyrsta Agate, [[General]] [[Tyben]], and [[Lieutenant General]] [[Brockway]]. ''Home One'' along with Agate's [[Starhawk-class battleship|''Starhawk''-class battleship]] ''[[Concord]]'' took part in the assault on the Imperial Star Destroyers enveloping the Imperial [[Super Star Destroyer]] ''[[Ravager]]'', which served as the Imperial command ship. From the bridge of ''Home One'', Ackbar watched as the ''Concord'' used its powerful [[tractor beam projector]] to drag the ''Ravager'' to [[Jakku]]'s surface. The battle was a victory for the New Republic.<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref>

===Resistance service===
Eventually, ''Home One'' was retired from service and was recruited by the Resistance.<ref name="BTA">''[[Before the Awakening]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
In the [[Star Wars Legends|old Expanded Universe]], the [[MC80a Star Cruiser|MC80a]] and [[MC80A Home One Type Heavy Star Cruiser/Legends|MC80 ''Home One'' type Star Cruiser]] were two separate models. This was changed, however, in the [[canon]] book ''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]'', which describes both designations belonging to the MC80.<ref name="AB Update" />

